{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ErrorComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" component renders an error notice and optional details about the thrown value."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"errorcomponent-props","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ErrorComponent props"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ErrorComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" component accepts the following props:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"props-error-prop","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.error"},{"type":"text","value":" prop"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":" in React and Vue; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Error"},{"type":"text","value":" in Solid"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The caught error. Solid normalizes non-"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Error"},{"type":"text","value":" values, including SSR loader errors, into an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Error"},{"type":"text","value":" with the original value in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cause"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"props-info-prop","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.info"},{"type":"text","value":" prop"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ componentStack: string }"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Additional information about where the error was thrown, such as the React component stack trace."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"props-reset-prop","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props.reset"},{"type":"text","value":" prop"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function to programmatically reset the error state"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"errorcomponent-returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ErrorComponent returns"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Displays an error notice, with details when the thrown value has a nonempty "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"message"},{"type":"text","value":". Values without a message still display the error notice."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The error message can be toggled by clicking the \"Show Error\" button."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the error message will be shown in development."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"errorcomponent-props","text":"ErrorComponent props","level":2},{"id":"props-error-prop","text":"props.error prop","level":3},{"id":"props-info-prop","text":"props.info prop","level":3},{"id":"props-reset-prop","text":"props.reset prop","level":3},{"id":"errorcomponent-returns","text":"ErrorComponent returns","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `ErrorComponent` component renders an error notice and optional details about the thrown value.\n\n## ErrorComponent props\n\nThe `ErrorComponent` component accepts the following props:\n\n### `props.error` prop\n\n- Type: `unknown` in React and Vue; `Error` in Solid\n- The caught error. Solid normalizes non-`Error` values, including SSR loader errors, into an `Error` with the original value in `cause`.\n\n### `props.info` prop\n\n- Type: `{ componentStack: string }`\n- Optional\n- Additional information about where the error was thrown, such as the React component stack trace.\n\n### `props.reset` prop\n\n- Type: `() => void`\n- A function to programmatically reset the error state\n\n## ErrorComponent returns\n\n- Displays an error notice, with details when the thrown value has a nonempty `message`. Values without a message still display the error notice.\n- The error message can be toggled by clicking the \"Show Error\" button.\n- By default, the error message will be shown in development.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: errorComponentComponent\ntitle: ErrorComponent component\n---\n\nThe `ErrorComponent` component renders an error notice and optional details about the thrown value.\n\n## ErrorComponent props\n\nThe `ErrorComponent` component accepts the following props:\n\n### `props.error` prop\n\n- Type: `unknown` in React and Vue; `Error` in Solid\n- The caught error. Solid normalizes non-`Error` values, including SSR loader errors, into an `Error` with the original value in `cause`.\n\n### `props.info` prop\n\n- Type: `{ componentStack: string }`\n- Optional\n- Additional information about where the error was thrown, such as the React component stack trace.\n\n### `props.reset` prop\n\n- Type: `() => void`\n- A function to programmatically reset the error state\n\n## ErrorComponent returns\n\n- Displays an error notice, with details when the thrown value has a nonempty `message`. Values without a message still display the error notice.\n- The error message can be toggled by clicking the \"Show Error\" button.\n- By default, the error message will be shown in development.\n"}
